{ A rook belongs on a useful file, not automatically on whichever file is empty. Look for a target, an entry square, and a safe route to that square. } 1. Rc1 Re8 2. Rc7 { Illustrative line. Rc1 places the rook on the open c-file. If Black continues ...Re8, White can invade with Rc7 and attack along the seventh rank. The sequence illustrates a route; ...Re8 is not forced, and Black could instead contest the c-file. Before invading, inspect the destination. A rook that reaches the seventh rank but can be captured has accomplished nothing. Here c7 is safe, and the rook can attack pawns from the side. That concrete target explains the file choice. } *

[Event "Give Every Piece a Job / 04.1B"]
